      "text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 19 #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Enhanced Southwest Monsoon (Habagat)\nIssued at: 2:00 AM, 24 September 2025(Wednesday)\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Zambales and Bataan.\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: Possible FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, expect light to moderate rains over Metro Manila, Quezon, Rizal and Laguna within the next 3 hours.\nLight to moderate rains affecting Pampanga, Tarlac(San Jose, Concepcion, Capas, Bamban, Tarlac City), Bulacan(San Miguel, San Ildefonso, San Rafael, Baliuag, Pulilan, Calumpit, Hagonoy, Paombong, Malolos, Plaridel), Nueva Ecija(San Antonio, Cabiao), Cavite(Maragondon, Ternate) and Batangas(Nasugbu) which may persist within 3 hours and may affect nearby areas.\n\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 5:00 AM today.\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
